1. DEFINITIONS

"CiAi" means the software, source code, documentation, and associated materials
in this repository that are owned or controlled by The Singularity Workshop.

"Licensee" means the individual or legal entity accepting this license. If the
Licensee is an entity, its parent entities, subsidiaries, and entities under
common control are included when calculating the repository allowance.

"Repository" means one distinct GitHub repository identified by its canonical
owner/name identity. Public and private repositories both count. A fork counts
as a separate Repository when CiAi is configured to operate on it.

"Configured Repository" means a Repository that the Licensee has enrolled,
configured, connected, or authorized CiAi to observe, assess, build against, or
otherwise process. A repository remains counted while it remains configured,
even if temporarily inactive or archived.

2. FREE INTERNAL-USE GRANT

Subject to compliance with this license, The Singularity Workshop grants the
Licensee a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free right to install, execute,
reproduce, and modify CiAi for the Licensee's own internal purposes on no more
than five (5) Configured Repositories at any one time.

The five-Repository allowance is available to individuals, educational and
non-profit projects, and commercial businesses on the same terms. The
allowance is not limited by employee count, revenue, or organization type.

3. ADDITIONAL REPOSITORIES REQUIRE A PAID LICENSE

The Licensee must obtain and maintain a paid commercial license before
configuring CiAi for a sixth Repository or any additional Repository beyond
the maximum number authorized by its paid entitlement.

Repository allowances are aggregated across the Licensee and its parent,
subsidiary, and commonly controlled entities, including their GitHub accounts
and organizations. Splitting repositories across accounts or organizations
does not create additional free allowances.

A paid license may specify a larger repository allowance, subscription term,
fees, and additional rights. The applicable order, subscription, or enterprise
agreement controls where it expressly supplements these terms.

